# Cloudflare Workers and Deployment

This app runs on Cloudflare Workers via `@opennextjs/cloudflare`, not on Node or Vercel.
Code must be compatible with the Workers runtime.

## Configuration

- Worker configuration lives in `wrangler.jsonc`. Note the `.jsonc` extension: comments are allowed.
- Worker `name` is `quizmaker`. That is the first label in `https://quizmaker.<account-subdomain>.workers.dev`.
- Keep `nodejs_compat` in `compatibility_flags`. OpenNext requires it for Next.js.
- Add resource bindings (D1, R2, KV, AI) to `wrangler.jsonc`, then run `npm run cf-typegen`
  to regenerate `cloudflare-env.d.ts` so the bindings are typed.
- Never edit `cloudflare-env.d.ts` by hand. It is generated.

## Runtime constraints

- No Node built-ins beyond what `nodejs_compat` provides. Avoid `fs` and native modules.
- Access bindings through `getCloudflareContext()` from `@opennextjs/cloudflare`,
  not through a global `env`.

## Secrets and environment

- Local values go in `.dev.vars`, which is gitignored. Keep `.dev.vars.example` current
  whenever a new variable is introduced.
- Production values are set with `npx wrangler secret put NAME`. Never commit a secret
  and never write one into `wrangler.jsonc`.

## workers.dev subdomain names

The account-level subdomain (the middle label in `https://quizmaker.<subdomain>.workers.dev`)
must match `^[a-z0-9]([a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?$`: lowercase letters, digits, hyphens;
no capitals, no underscores. Wrangler re-prompts silently if the name is invalid.
Register it in the user's interactive terminal or the Cloudflare dashboard. A non-interactive
agent shell will default that prompt to **no**.

## Deployment

- `npm run preview` builds and runs the app on the local Workers runtime. Prefer this over
  `npm run dev` when verifying anything runtime-specific, since `npm run dev` uses Node.
- `npm run deploy` builds and deploys with `wrangler deploy` (also POSTs the Worker workers.dev route).
- `npm run upload` builds and uploads a Worker version without enabling the workers.dev route.
- Do not run `npm run deploy` unless the user explicitly asks you to deploy.
- If deploy uploads the Worker then fails with API **10034** on
  `POST .../workers/scripts/quizmaker/subdomain` while the dashboard already shows a verified
  email, use `npm run upload` and enable workers.dev in the dashboard. Relogin does not fix it.
- OpenNext warns that Windows is unsupported; builds on this repo have still succeeded.
